<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Imphold lifts yr share, dividend.</title>
<headline>Imphold lifts yr share, dividend.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr ended June 25 1996.</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, post-exceps (cts) 170.1    vs   115.9</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		   68.0    vs    45.0</p>
<p>    Headline earnings	245.8    vs   121.7</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  0.5    vs     0.8</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    360.5    vs   201.5</p>
<p>    Tax			  120.4    vs    71.8</p>
<p>    Turnover		 6,421.6    vs 2,667.8</p>
<p>Div payable: October 29</p>
<p>On register: September 20</p>
<p>Full name: Imperial Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters had forecast EPS of 172.7 cents, with the range 170.4-175.0, and a dividend of 67.5, with a range 66.6-68.4.</p>
<p>The company said shareholders would be awarded capitalisation shares in the ratio of 0,89655 new ordinary shares for every 100 shares held. It said shareholders could instead elect to receive a cash dividend.</p>
<p>The company also said it was budgeting for good growth in the year to June 1997 from its present high base.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
